  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "Which image generator is cheapest at scale?",
      "answer": "Self-hosted FLUX.1 / SDXL on a rented RTX 4090 is usually cheapest above a few thousand images per month because you pay for GPU time, not per generation. Among hosted APIs, Stability AI SDXL and Ideogram are typically the lowest per-image for standard 1024×1024 generations."
    },
    {
      "question": "Does Midjourney have an official API?",
      "answer": "Midjourney does not have a first-party public API. Most integrations use a Discord-bot proxy or unofficial API services, which is why pricing is approximate and often subscription-based."
    },
    {
      "question": "How do I account for prompting cost?",
      "answer": "Many production pipelines use an LLM to rewrite or expand prompts before generating images. The calculator adds prompt-input and prompt-output tokens multiplied by your chosen model's per-million-token price."
    },
    {
      "question": "What about human review and curation?",
      "answer": "Set a review rate (percentage of images a human checks) and minutes per review. The calculator multiplies that by the reviewer's hourly cost to estimate QA labor."
    },
    {
      "question": "When is local/self-hosted worth it?",
      "answer": "Self-hosting wins on volume, latency, and privacy. It loses if you need the absolute latest model quality, do not want to manage drivers/updates, or generate only a few hundred images per month."
    }
